{"cuisine/shippoku":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/shippoku","n":"Shippoku","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Japanese Chinese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Japan","intro":[["Shippoku is a Japanese culinary style that is heavily influenced by Chinese cuisine. It has been described as a fusion cuisine and as a \"hybrid cuisine\" that combines elements of European, Chinese and Japanese cuisines. Meats used in shippoku cuisine include fowl, fish, and game meats. Sake typically accompanies shippoku dishes. The shippoku style of service typically includes several small dishes that comprise a full meal."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"shippoku"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shippoku"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Japanese Chinese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Japanese Chinese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6e/Nagasaki_Shippoku_Hamakatsu01s.jpg/500px-Nagasaki_Shippoku_Hamakatsu01s.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"663highland","lic":"CC BY 2.5","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagasaki_Shippoku_Hamakatsu01s.jpg"}},"cuisine/azerbaijani-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/azerbaijani-cuisine","n":"Azerbaijani cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Caucasian cuisine","cuisine/caucasian-cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Azerbaijan","intro":[["Azerbaijani cuisine is a term describing the cooking styles and dishes of the Republic of Azerbaijan. The cuisine is influenced by the country's agriculture that mostly developed on grasslands allowing a culture of pastoralism to develop, as well as to the geographical location of the country, which is situated between Europe and Asia with access to the Caspian Sea. This location has enabled the people that now live in the territory of Azerbaijan to develop a diet rich in produce, milk products, and meat, including beef, mutton, fish and game. The location, which was contested by many historical kingdoms, khanates, and empires, also meant that Azerbaijani cuisine was influenced by the culinary traditions of multiple different cultures, including Turkic, Iranian, Armenian and Eastern European cuisines. Many dishes of Armenian cuisine and Georgian cuisine with Turkified or Turkic names are widespread in Azerbaijan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"azerbaijani-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azerbaijani_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Caucasian cuisine","cuisine/caucasian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Pomegranates & Saffron: A Culinary Journey to Azerbaijan","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Feride Buyuran, 2015","note":"Large collection of Azerbaijani recipes with cultural background.","url":"","suggested":true},{"name":"Kaukasis: A Culinary Journey through Georgia, Azerbaijan & Beyond","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Olia Hercules, 2017","note":"Recipes gathered across the Caucasus, mostly Georgia and Azerbaijan.","url":"https://www.simonandschuster.ca/books/Kaukasis/Olia-Hercules/9781681883038","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781681883038"}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":12,"links":[["Badambura","dish/badambura"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Doghramaj","dish/doghramaj"],["Dovga","dish/dovga"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Scorched rice","dish/scorched-rice"],["Shekerbura","dish/shekerbura"],["Sheki halva","dish/sheki-halva"],["Shorgoghal","dish/shorgoghal"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Syrup","ingredient/syrup"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Hazelnut","ingredient/hazelnut"],["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Ayran","ingredient/ayran"],["Dill","ingredient/dill"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Mentha","ingredient/mentha"],["Qatiq","ingredient/qatiq"],["Spinach","ingredient/spinach"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Rumen","ingredient/rumen"],["Animal fats and oils","ingredient/animal-fats-and-oils"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Dried fruit","ingredient/dried-fruit"],["Lard","ingredient/lard"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Caucasian cuisine","cuisine/caucasian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/5f/Azerbaijan_Light_snack.jpg/500px-Azerbaijan_Light_snack.jpg","w":500,"h":394,"by":"Emin Bashirov","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Azerbaijan_Light_snack.jpg"}},"cuisine/frisian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/frisian-cuisine","n":"Frisian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Germany","intro":[["Frisian cuisine consists of the traditional recipes and cooking methods of the historic region of Frisia, which is in present-day Germany and the Netherlands. Frisian cuisine is diverse, drawing from both land and sea. Most dishes, excluding desserts, are made of fish or potatoes, though there are several dishes based on other ingredients. Especially in West Frisia, the food resembles that of the Dutch Cuisine, though East Frisia and North Frisia present dishes that are very much unique to the region."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"frisian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frisian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine"},"ingredient/linguica":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/linguica","n":"Linguiça","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Linguiça is a Portuguese sausage made from pork and seasoned with onion, garlic, paprika and other spices. It can be used fresh in cooked preparations or undergo a curing and preservation process through smoking."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-linguica"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lingui%C3%A7a"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Brazilian cuisine","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",[["Arroz carreteiro","dish/arroz-carreteiro"]]],["Portuguese cuisine","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",[["Francesinha","dish/francesinha"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Carne-seca","ingredient/carne-seca"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Parsley","ingredient/parsley"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Beer","ingredient/beer"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Chipolata","ingredient/chipolata"],["Ham","ingredient/ham"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/65/Linguicabrazil.jpg/500px-Linguicabrazil.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Camila e Sérgio Paganini Staut","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Linguicabrazil.jpg"}},"dish/bear-paw":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bear-paw","n":"Bear paw","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Bear hunting is a practice that has been historically present in every culture in contact with the animal. Bears have been hunted since prehistoric times for their meat and fur. In addition to being a source of food, in modern times they have been favored by big game hunters due to their size and ferocity. Bear hunting has a vast history throughout Europe and North America, and hunting practices have varied based on location and type of bear."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bear-paw"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_paw"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Red House Spice","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Dandan noodles","dish/dandan-noodles"],["Dapanji","dish/dapanji"],["Dong'an chicken","dish/dong-an-chicken"],["Dongpo pork","dish/dongpo-pork"],["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Drunken shrimp","dish/drunken-shrimp"],["Edible bird's nest","dish/edible-bird-s-nest"],["Fish sauce","dish/fish-sauce"],["Fuqi feipian","dish/fuqi-feipian"],["Gaifan","dish/gaifan"],["Goubuli","dish/goubuli"],["Hainanese chicken rice","dish/hainanese-chicken-rice"],["Hog maw","dish/hog-maw"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"],["Hot pot","dish/hot-pot"],["Huangqiao sesame cake","dish/huangqiao-sesame-cake"],["Imitation shark fin soup","dish/imitation-shark-fin-soup"],["Jiaozi","dish/jiaozi"],["Jiuqu","dish/jiuqu"],["Kung Pao chicken","dish/kung-pao-chicken"],["Lanzhou beef noodles","dish/lanzhou-beef-noodles"],["Liangfen","dish/liangfen"],["Lo mai chi","dish/lo-mai-chi"],["Mao xue wang","dish/mao-xue-wang"],["Mapo tofu","dish/mapo-tofu"],["Mianwo","dish/mianwo"],["Miso soup","dish/miso-soup"],["Orange cuttlefish","dish/orange-cuttlefish"],["Osmanthus cake","dish/osmanthus-cake"],["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/11/Suspected_smuggled_air-dried_bear_paws.jpg/500px-Suspected_smuggled_air-dried_bear_paws.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Fumikas Sagisavas","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suspected_smuggled_air-dried_bear_paws.jpg"}},"ingredient/sultana-grape":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sultana-grape","n":"Sultana (grape)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["The sultana is a \"white\" (pale green), oval seedless grape variety also called the sultanina, Thompson Seedless (United States), Lady de Coverly (England), and oval-fruited Kishmish (Iran, Iraq, Palestine, Pakistan, Afghanistan, India). It is also known as a grape found in İzmir, or Manisa in Turkey, since this variety has been extensively grown in the region around those cities. It is assumed to originate from Asia Minor, which later became part of the Ottoman Empire."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sultana-grape"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultana_(grape)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Dundee cake","dish/dundee-cake"]]],["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine",[["Oliebol","dish/oliebol"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Currant","ingredient/currant"],["Seville orange","ingredient/seville-orange"],["Baking powder","ingredient/baking-powder"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Ribes","ingredient/ribes"],["Succade","ingredient/succade"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Zest","ingredient/zest"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/85/Thompson_seedless_grapes.JPG/500px-Thompson_seedless_grapes.JPG","w":500,"h":331,"by":"Glane23","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thompson_seedless_grapes.JPG"}},"ingredient/solanaceae":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/solanaceae","n":"Solanaceae","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Solanaceae (), commonly known as the nightshades, is a family of flowering plants in the order Solanales. The family contains approximately 2,700 species, several of which are used as agricultural crops, medicinal plants, and ornamental plants. Many members of the family have high alkaloid contents, making some highly toxic, but many—such as tomatoes, potatoes, eggplants and peppers—are commonly used in food around the world."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-solanaceae"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanaceae"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Karedok","dish/karedok"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Cucumber","ingredient/cucumber"],["Holy basil","ingredient/holy-basil"],["Kencur","ingredient/kencur"],["Krupuk","ingredient/krupuk"],["Mung bean sprout","ingredient/mung-bean-sprout"],["Pachyrhizus erosus","ingredient/pachyrhizus-erosus"],["Peanut sauce","ingredient/peanut-sauce"],["Shrimp paste","ingredient/shrimp-paste"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8b/Brugmansia_lg.jpg/500px-Brugmansia_lg.jpg","w":500,"h":350,"by":"Unknown author","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brugmansia_lg.jpg"}},"dish/kue-rangi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kue-rangi","n":"Kue rangi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kue rangi or also called sagu rangi is an Indonesian coconut kue or traditional snack made of a  coconut and starch-based batter and cooked in a special molded pan. It is one of the traditional Betawi snack of Jakarta. Kue rangi is often described as Indonesian coconut waffle."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kue-rangi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kue_rangi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["